!!! Checked byte spans. Empty spans at the end are valid; invalid bounds
!!! return None. These operations do not decode Unicode characters.
book nil.std.text

read everything from nil.std.core

public try-substring receives s as text, start as override long, length as override long returns Option of text begin paragraph
    value size as override long is (the length of s) becomes override long
    when start is less than 0 or start is greater than size or length is less than 0 then
        give Option.None
    end when
    !!! Validate before subtraction; adding start and length could overflow.
    when length is greater than (size minus start) then
        give Option.None
    end when
    give Option.Some holding (s.substr with start being start, length being length)
end paragraph

public try-char-at receives s as text, index as override long returns Option of text begin paragraph
    give try-substring with s being s, start being index, length being 1
end paragraph
